key line: `iadd $llr0 $lls0 $lls16` -> 0000000b 0000000b 00000002 00000002
  = 1+10 in lanes 0,1 (cycle 0's MSB long word) and 2,2 = GRF0 words 2,3
  passed through, NOT 1+10.  So `ll` gives 2 computed int32 lanes per
  cycle, i.e. 8 per instruction word, for every arithmetic opcode.
